      "value": "I'm probably asking a dumb question here, but wouldn't simply delivering a .unitypackage file be the safer alternative, as well as giving the client the rights to the avatar so they could edit it later if they wish? Clients wouldn't need to give out their login information and they could control who has access to their avatar.\nFor the case like Major stated, having a way to share a private avatar with a select few that you authorize would be great.",
